cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this construction and formal verification, identify the commit consulted, and retain the prior-construction credits."
title: "A Covering Array with 86 Rows, 40 Columns, and Three Symbols"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ozols
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://github.com/cozuya"
url: "https://cozuya.github.io/improvements/covering-array-86-3-40-3"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/covering-array-86-3-40-3"
abstract: >-
  An explicit CA(86;3,40,3) with a Lean 4.28.0 kernel-checked proof of
  CAN(3,40,3) <= 86. It improves the best previously located public upper
  bound from 87 to 86 according to a supplied prior-art audit with research
  cutoff November 14, 2026. The construction was obtained by postoptimizing
  Bai XunDi's 87-row extension of the Shokri–Moura lineage. By Chris Ozols,
  with AI-assisted construction, verification, and formalization. All 266,760
  coverage requirements are checked with decide +kernel; there is no native
  evaluation axiom and no Mathlib dependency. Optimality and absolute
  historical priority are not established. Third-party material retains its
  original license; see NOTICE.
keywords:
  - covering array
  - combinatorial design
  - combinatorial testing
  - ternary array
  - upper bound
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
